Generate a detailed curriculum for teaching "{{ topic }}" at a {{ depth }} level of depth.

Respond with a JSON object containing two lists: "prerequisites" (things the student should know before starting) and "main_curriculum" (the actual lessons to teach).

Each lesson must have:
- "id": a string like "0.1", "1.2" (prerequisites use 0.x, main curriculum uses 1.x)
- "title": a concise title
- "description": a 1-2 sentence description of what the lesson covers

Guidelines:
- Prerequisites should be 2-4 items covering foundational concepts.
- Main curriculum should be 6-10 lessons, ordered from fundamentals to advanced topics.
- Adjust the number of lessons and their complexity to match {{ depth }} depth.
- Lessons should build on each other progressively.
- Include practical examples and industry applications where relevant.

Respond with ONLY the JSON object, no other text.

Example format:
```json
{
  "prerequisites": [
    {"id": "0.1", "title": "Basic Algebra", "description": "Solving equations and working with variables."}
  ],
  "main_curriculum": [
    {"id": "1.1", "title": "Introduction to {{ topic }}", "description": "Overview and core concepts."}
  ]
}
```
